#Working Directory
→ The place on your computer where you work on the project
  and make changes to files.

        ↓ git add

Staging Area
→ A place where you select the changes you want to include
  in the next commit.

        ↓ git commit

Local Repository
→ The Git repository stored on your computer (.git).
  It stores your committed project history.

        ↓ git push

Remote Repository
→ A Git repository hosted on a remote platform such as
  GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket.




#Short mental model

Work → Select → Commit → Share

Working Directory
      ↓
Staging Area
      ↓
Local Repository
      ↓
Remote Repository




#Simple distinction

"Maine code change kiya" → Working Directory

"Maine change commit kiya" → Local Repository
